# Docker build-context exclusions (audit-3 R3-DEP-F1).
#
# The glm-ocr service builds with `context: .` (the repo ROOT) because its
# Dockerfile lives under docker/glm-ocr/. Without this file every build
# transmitted the ENTIRE working tree to the daemon — including `.env.local`
# and `.env.production.local`, which holds the hosted Supabase SERVICE-ROLE
# key. That is context transmission (the Dockerfile has no COPY), but it still
# ships secrets and multi-GB build output over the socket on every build,
# which is expensive on a remote/WSL2 `DOCKER_HOST` and a needless exposure on
# a shared build daemon. The sibling insightface service avoids the problem by
# using `context: ./docker/insightface`; this file gives glm-ocr the same
# protection without restructuring the build.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the repo's actual generated/secret paths.

# Secrets — never send to the daemon.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.example

# Dependencies / build output
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Test + coverage artifacts
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
snapshots
bench-glm-ocr.jsonl

# Large / irrelevant trees that the build context was paying for on EVERY build
# (defect: measured 41+ MB of context uploaded per build). These matter because
# the Dockerfile has a `COPY . .` (build stage), so whatever survives this file
# is BOTH uploaded to the daemon AND copied into the build stage — excluding it
# here is what keeps it out of both. Verified: `git grep -n "COPY" Dockerfile`
# shows the only whole-context copy is `COPY . .`; the rest are targeted
# (package.json/package-lock.json, `--from=build` artifacts, exceljs).
#   - e2e            (4.2 MB) Playwright specs; the Dockerfile ALSO prunes the
#                    copy Next's tracer drags into .next/standalone
#   - screenshots    (37 MB)  explore-script dumps
#   - .zcode                  agent session artifacts
#   - invoice_*               customer invoices (a real document, not test data)
e2e
screenshots
.zcode
invoice_edited.html
invoice_from_html.pdf

# Runtime state that must NEVER enter an image layer (VPS deployment).
# These are written by the running app / ops scripts on the HOST, and the app
# Dockerfile builds with `context: .` — so without these lines a later
# `docker build` would copy host runtime state (including the spend ledger's
# per-user token accounting and the prod-destructive audit trail) into the
# build context, and `COPY . .` would bake it into a layer.
#   - .prod-audit.log          : destructive-script audit trail (scripts/lib/remote-env.mjs)
#   - .glm-spend-ledger.json*  : per-user daily OCR token/spend ledger (WS-CORE
#     glm-spend.ts). The GLOB is load-bearing, not defensive: the ledger is
#     written tmp-then-rename (`.glm-spend-ledger.json.tmp`, glm-spend.ts:258),
#     so the exact-name rule alone left the temp sibling matching — a crash
#     mid-write leaves that file holding the day's accounting, and it would then
#     ride into the build context (and a `COPY . .`) unignored.
.prod-audit.log*
.glm-spend-ledger.json*

# SOPS secrets (deploy/secrets/). The app Dockerfile builds with `context: .`
# and does `COPY . .` (Dockerfile:83), so anything present under the repo root
# rides into a build layer. The plaintext `prod.env` is gitignored and normally
# exists only ON THE VPS — but the failure this guards is a developer running
# `sops -d` in place, or `bootstrap.sh`, on the machine doing the build. Without
# these lines the service-role key, the Z.ai key and the sidecar token would be
# baked into a layer, where `docker save` can read them even if a later layer
# deletes the file.
#
# `*.enc` (the committed ciphertext) is excluded too: harmless to publish, but
# useless inside the image, and shipping it only creates a way for an unrelated
# layer diff to reveal when secrets were rotated.
deploy/secrets/prod.env
deploy/secrets/prod.env.local
deploy/secrets/*.agekey
deploy/secrets/*.key
deploy/secrets/*.enc
# Belt-and-braces: any env file under deploy/ at all.
deploy/**/.env
deploy/**/.env.local

# Local Supabase / tooling data
supabase/.temp
supabase/.branches
compreface-data

# VCS + agent scratch
.git
.gitignore
.github
.agents
.vscode
.idea
.tmp
.tmp_*

# Docs / design scratch (not needed by any Dockerfile today)
docs
design-system
redesign-previews
Sample Code
graphify-out
skills-lock.json
GEMINI.md
PROJECT.md
AGENTS.md

# Python bytecode (the insightface build context is its own dir, but keep the
# root context clean if a future Dockerfile builds from here).
__pycache__
*.pyc

# Misc editor/OS noise
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
